# Recognition of the binary triple Mathieu module

James's theorem supplies existence, the degree-twelve uniqueness equivalence,
and the minimum degree for the genuine triple cover. The central cubic
operator supplies compatible F₄ scalars of dimension six, with an actual
scalar-restriction equivalence. The restriction bridge proves that a faithful
irreducible ambient module of binary dimension twelve is the unique component
module when F*(G) is that triple cover.

The native unitary realization transports through the same field-linear
intertwiner, providing the nondegenerate invariant Hermitian form and its
invariant binary quadratic diagonal on every such module. The faithful
homomorphism into the literal SU₆(2) model, its binary coordinates, and their
scalar and form identities discharge the unitary input of the local calculation.
Thus H.12.1(1–2) is established with no extra premises. For H.12.1(3), the
separate displacement theorem must still supply the dimension bound before
applying the restriction bridge.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith H.12.1(1–3), printed pp.393–394 (PDF pp.404–405).
-/
